  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Solid Lead nitrate is dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;litre of water. The solution was found to boil at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> is added to the resulting solution, it was observed that the solution froze at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The solutbility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;formed is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume molality to be equal to molarity in all cases.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let a mole <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pb</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be added, dissociation of lead nitrate will result in:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>Pb</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8594;</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>&#8710;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>Pb</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>PbCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br />During reformation of lead nitrate as a precipitate,<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>Pb</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>PbCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>&nbsp;....(i)</p><p>In final solution after addition of 0.2 moles of sodium and chloride ions:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>From (i),<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><msup><mo>]</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>27</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>27</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
